 ent start. Please register ahead of the event. Registrants will receive Z
 oom information and related materials by email one week and within 24 hou
 rs before the event.</i>\n\nReserve your seat in the virtual Research Int
 egrity Roundtable "Whose Paper Is It Anyway? Good and Questionable Author
 ship Practices" on August 11th\, 2026 from 2:00 pm - 3:30 pm. Participant
 s will learn about good and questionable authorship practices\, the Duke 
 guidelines regarding authorship\, and what to do when you have an authors
 hip dispute. A case study will be discussed in breakout rooms.\n\nThis ev
 ent is only open to current Duke faculty\, staff\, and students. Attendin
 g this event fulfills the <b>RCR-200</b> requirement for Faculty and Staf
 f as well as the <b>714 RCR credit</b> for graduate students\, but partic
 ipants must attend for at least 60 minutes to receive credit.\n\n\nContac
 t:\nASIST\nasist@duke.edu
DURATION:PT1H30M
